From 47c28aca511a64bb5a3c54a440508e0ec1b3f070 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:19:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(2d): Side Auto reads the material at the picked
 ring's own level

Side Auto of a 2D Contour on picked rings read the full XY silhouette
of the part. The floor of a blind bore fills that silhouette, so Auto
resolved Outside on a bore rim and the #1927 law refused the pass.

The new law (machining2d::auto_side) reads the part section just under
the top of the picks' Z span, then just over its bottom, and compares
the area inside the rings with a 0.5 mm band outside them. Material on
one side only decides the side. Probes that disagree, or material on
both sides or on neither, refuse the generate by name and ask for
Inside or Outside.

Fixes #1933

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
